  "id": "Compound::DB00703 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Methazolamide is shown to bind to Cyp2c19, a cytochrome P450 enzyme, which participates in the oxidation of limonene derivatives. This binding and participation are consistent across three distinct paths, each identifying Cyp2c19 as a participant in different forms of limonene monooxygenase activity—specifically (r)-limonene 6-monooxygenase and (s)-limonene 7-monooxygenase. These activities are ultimately linked to Cyp2c9, suggesting a potential mechanism where Methazolamide influences the activity of Cyp2c19, which in turn modulates the activity of Cyp2c9. The evidence supports a functional relationship where Methazolamide may affect Cyp2c9 through its interaction with Cyp2c19, which is involved in the metabolic activation of limonene derivatives. The consistency of the scores across the three paths indicates a robust, albeit indirect, connection between Methazolamide and Cyp2c9, highlighting the role of Cyp2c19 as a critical mediator in this relationship.",
